            "notes": "**POWER 3:**\n\nNormally, I take [Hyper Healer](item_108336b3-54d2-4d69-8ea4-c2da5affb7ca) for the extra support to my team. The extra overhealth makes Hyper Ring an even better engage/disengage ability. It can also come in very clutch between reloading and waiting for Pulsar Torpedoes.\n\nIf your team is already well supported, you can consider taking [Torpedo Glide](item_b04180a3-c2b2-409c-959e-77e3af6bc7d8) for even more cooldown on Pulsar Torpedos. \n\n[Medicinal Missiles](item_30eeab6c-4a1e-4a16-b9dd-e83d633caa40) can also be considered to help team survival, especially if your other support is struggling to put out heals.\n\n**ITEMS**\n\nNormally, I would take [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) as it pairs well with this build and Juno in general. Constantly repairing shield or armor whenever you use a Pulsar Torpedo or Speed Ring.\n\n[Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) is another great option. Since you need to be at full health for its overhealth effect to build up, I would say [Lumerico Fusion Drive](item_3da81000-333c-460a-a1a2-09441bfda9c8) is the safer option. But if you're not taking much damage, it can be a solid option for a slight Mediblaster boost.",
