            "created_at": "2025-08-16T09:18:20.795908+00:00",
            "notes": "POWER 4:\n\nMy choice is usually [Torpedo Glide](item_b04180a3-c2b2-409c-959e-77e3af6bc7d8). When used correctly, you can throw out 3-4 Pulsar Torpedoes in quick succession. \n\nIf you took [Torpedo Glide](item_b04180a3-c2b2-409c-959e-77e3af6bc7d8) round 5, [Hyper Healer](item_108336b3-54d2-4d69-8ea4-c2da5affb7ca) is still a strong option.\n\n[Medicinal Missiles](item_30eeab6c-4a1e-4a16-b9dd-e83d633caa40) should be taken if you feel your team might struggle against a round 7 buffed enemy team.\n\nIf you're feeling crazy, you might even try [Rally Ring](item_0547012b-4817-437e-aad3-aa37db93383e) to have more [Hyper Healer](item_108336b3-54d2-4d69-8ea4-c2da5affb7ca) uptime. \n\n**ITEMS:**\n\n[Phantasmic Flux](item_5e644a79-cf6e-4196-8d0a-232f75004643) is the usual choice. It's round 7, heroes are going to hit like a truck, and a solid survival item will make a big difference.\n\nIf you prefer the glass cannon approach, [Pulsar Destroyers](item_707ad8c7-a153-4140-b4bc-1f23f7d7a648) will help delete the enemy team.\n\n**You should sell [Multi-Tool](item_5ba8d94e-f2f3-44b7-8773-025fc6ed7c56) and replace it with [Pulsar Destroyers](item_707ad8c7-a153-4140-b4bc-1f23f7d7a648) if you have the cash to do so.**",
